Author: kirkouimet <kirk@kirkouimet.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 7 00:16:47 2026 -0600

    rules: a pattern a user wrote in a rule's options compiles as JavaScript reads it, not as RE2 (#7mztrdd)
    
    A rule's option pattern is written by its user as a JavaScript regexp, and upstream compiles it with `new
    RegExp(pattern, flags)`. 17 sites across 15 rules compiled it with Go's RE2, which refuses lookahead, lookbehind
    and backreferences (so the option was dropped or the config refused) and reads `\s` without the no-break space,
    the byte order mark and 18 more, among other gaps. They now compile through esregexp with upstream's own flags:
    
    - `u`: no-inline-comments ignorePattern, no-param-reassign ignorePropertyModificationsForRegex, default-case
      commentPattern, id-length exceptionPatterns, object-shorthand methodsIgnorePattern, id-match pattern,
      no-unused-vars' four ignore patterns, switch-exhaustiveness-check defaultCaseCommentPattern,
      no-require-imports allow;
    - `iu`: no-warning-comments (its pattern built from the user's terms), and no-fallthrough commentPattern, which
      keeps oxc's case-insensitivity in JavaScript's dialect;
    - none: exhaustive-deps additionalHooks, boolean-prop-naming rule, enforce-canonical-classes ignore (shared with
      no-unknown-classes, which upstream compiles the same way);
    - the user's own: sort-comp's `/body/flags` entries, so `u` and `y` now count (a fresh sticky regexp anchors).
    The rules' default patterns that share a variable (default-case's and switch-exhaustiveness-check's `/^no
    default$/iu`) compile through esregexp with upstream's flags too. The one RE2 site left in the class is
    no-unstable-nested-components, whose upstream matches a minimatch glob rather than a regexp.
    
    Each use takes the esregexp method by which way a match that overruns the time bound should fall: TestOrTimeout
    where a match spares a report (an ignore, allow, exception or excusing comment, a name required to match), Test
    where it causes one. Two rules used one pattern both ways and now ask each way: no-fallthrough's matcher returns
    one predicate for a fallthrough it excuses and one for an unused comment it reports, and
    switch-exhaustiveness-check carries whether a default comment's match overran, so it is not reported as the
    dangerous default it would be had it matched.
    
    no-warning-comments also escapes as upstream's escape-string-regexp does, `-` as `\x2d`, so a `-` decoration is
    one character rather than a range (`*`, `-`, `/` took in `+`), and its first-character fast path skips
    JavaScript's whitespace (text.IsWhitespace), the class the pattern now compiles. That closes the first instance
    #tez6dna names.
    
    Fixtures: every rule gains the case RE2 read differently, checked in Node: a lookahead or lookbehind that now
    takes effect, `\s` on U+00A0 where the subject can hold one, and a control the new pattern does not match. sort-comp's
    upstream invalid[9], held out as a recorded RE2 divergence, is a plain row now with upstream's own message, and its
    new rows were run through eslint-plugin-react 7.37.5 (all five agree). Three existing tests that pinned the RE2 drop (no-param-reassign, no-require-imports, sort-comp)
    now expect JavaScript's reading. Two overrun fixtures, `(a|aa)+$` on a long run of `a`, hold the two-way splits.
    Mutated:
    - esregexp refusing lookaround, as RE2 does: every rule's new fixtures fail, eight core rules run one by one;
    - no-fallthrough naming an unused comment on an overrun, or switch-exhaustiveness-check reporting one: each overrun
      fixture fails;
    - no-warning-comments without the `-` escape, or skipping Go's five whitespace characters: the lead test fails.
    
    Review, every rule on, each tree's own config, main 7945d102 against this, no tree changed: no finding moved on
    ahra (6), www (10), api (0), ahra-ai (0) or live www-phi-health (9,632). None of these options is configured by a
    consumer's settings or a shipped set, so none could. The docs recapture (`generate -capture`, 42,860 records)
    changed no file: the new cases run with options, which are counted and not shown.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Ahra <ahra@ahra.ai>
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

